    {
      "name": "staff_rudeness_or_indifference",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A meaningful service-quality axis that plausibly predicts dissatisfaction and gives a real grouping variable. Grounded on most rows (rows 1-4 correct), but row 5 flags rudeness/indifference where the source describes discriminatory door policy and giving away a cabana rather than staff rudeness per se; a mild overreach, so slightly reduced groundedness."
    },
    {
      "name": "excessive_wait_or_slow_service",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Distinct, analytically useful signal for predicting low satisfaction. Sampled values are sound: row 2's repeated forgetting implies waiting, others correctly False. Well grounded in the text."
    },
    {
      "name": "staff_inattention_or_neglect",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Useful behavioral axis, though it overlaps heavily with staff_forgot_or_ignored_table, slightly reducing incremental leverage. Values are well supported (row 2 neglect correctly True, others False)."
    },
    {
      "name": "poor_taste_or_flavor",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Captures a food-quality dimension orthogonal to the service columns, a genuinely different axis for the query. Sampled values are correct, including False for reviews that praise or don't mention flavor."
    },
    {
      "name": "staff_forgot_or_ignored_table",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.6,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Grounded and query-relevant (row 2 explicitly forgotten twice, correctly True), but it is a near-subset of staff_inattention_or_neglect, so its independent analytical contribution is limited by redundancy."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
  "source_groundedness": 0.87,
  "rationale": "The added columns decompose negative-experience drivers (rudeness, wait, inattention, food quality, being forgotten) that directly bear on predicting low Yelp satisfaction, giving real axes to compare against label_pos. Usefulness is somewhat diluted by overlap among the three staff-attention columns (inattention vs. forgot/ignored), but each still offers analytical value. Groundedness is strong across sampled rows, with the main weakness being an arguable over-flag of rudeness on row 5 where the complaint is about discriminatory admission rather than staff manner. No systematic invention of facts observed."
}

